Looking for an all in one wedding rental package in Malaga, Spain? Malaga Event Gear's [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) bundles the audio visual side of your day into one price and one delivery: PA sound, ambient lighting, wireless microphones and a live technician on site, all quoted, booked and installed as a single package rather than four separate rentals.

"All in one" is worth being precise about, though. It means one AV supplier handling sound, lighting, microphones and technical support together. It does not mean venue, catering, furniture or photography are part of the package, and any provider who implies otherwise is bundling trades that are not actually theirs. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview.

## Brief Overview

---

The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) is Malaga Event Gear's all in one AV package for weddings: a high end active PA system for up to 80 guests, fairy light and warm LED ambient lighting, wireless microphones for vows and speeches, and a live technician on site throughout, for 650 euros ex VAT. One quote, one delivery, one team on site, covering sound, lighting, microphones and technical support together.

## Key Highlights

---

-   One package, one price, for PA sound, ambient lighting, wireless microphones and a live technician.
-   650 euros ex VAT, sized for up to 80 guests, with delivery, setup and teardown included.
-   A live technician on site for the whole event, one of only two packages in our catalog that includes one.
-   The package covers AV equipment only: no venue, catering, furniture or photography.

## What "All in One" Means for the Wedding Pack

Booking AV equipment piece by piece from different suppliers means separate quotes, separate delivery windows and separate people to coordinate with on the day. The Wedding Pack removes that by putting sound, lighting, microphones and a technician under one booking with one supplier: we deliver, install, test and collect the equipment ourselves, so there is a single point of contact if anything needs adjusting between the ceremony and the reception.

That single point of contact matters most during the event itself. A technician who has been on site since setup already knows your run of show, so adjusting sound levels between the ceremony, speeches and dancing does not mean explaining the day's timeline to someone new each time.

