## What's Included, at 650 Euros

The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) costs 650 euros, ex VAT, with Spain's 21 percent VAT added at checkout. It includes:

-   A high end active PA sound system for up to 80 guests.
-   Fairy lights and warm LED strings for ambient lighting.
-   Professional wireless microphones for speeches and announcements.
-   Transport in Malaga and surrounding areas.
-   Professional setup and cabling.
-   A live technician on site throughout the event.
-   Post event teardown and pickup.

See exact, live pricing and the full breakdown on our [packages page](/packages/). If keeping the total down matters more than the technician, our guide on [cutting your AV rental costs](/blog/tips-for-reducing-wedding-rental-costs/) breaks down why the smaller Eco Pack is the single biggest lever available. For the booking pattern behind why couples pick the Wedding Pack over the Eco Pack, see our [latest trends in wedding rentals](/blog/latest-trends-in-wedding-rentals/) guide.

## What "All in One" Doesn't Cover

The Wedding Pack has no projector, screen or LED display, since a wedding rarely needs one. Furniture, decor and dancefloor accessories are not part of it or of our own inventory, and neither are cameras, filming or photography. If a package elsewhere claims to bundle all of that into one AV rental, ask for an itemized breakdown, since AV equipment and those other trades are typically separate services delivered by separate businesses. Our [questions to ask a wedding rental company](/blog/questions-to-ask-wedding-rental-companies/) guide covers how to get that breakdown from any provider you're comparing.

One package covering everything is not the same as one conversation covering everything, though. If your venue or planner leaves a gap, a dance floor, a backdrop or anything else, you can still tell us about it. We will enquire with suppliers about that gap for your date. If a supplier comes through, it appears as a separate line, not folded into the Wedding Pack as if it were ours.

